<title>UK: EU to import 85,000 T raw sugar a year for Finland.</title>
<headline>EU to import 85,000 T raw sugar a year for Finland.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union is expected to import just over 85,000 tonnes of raw sugar annually up to the year 2001 as a result of Finland's accession as a full member state, a senior sugar industry official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The raws imports would mainly come from Cuba and Brazil, but also some other nations, said Patricia Jamieson, divisional director for raw sugar and EEC affairs at leading UK trade house Tate &amp; Lyle.</p>
<p>Finland's obligations under the World Trade Organisation (WTO), which include imports of raws for refining, had now been consolidated into the EU's schedules, Jamieson told a two-day conference hosted by Agra Europe.</p>
<p>Four member states -- Finland, France, Portugal and the United Kingdom -- are desingated by the EU as refiners of raw sugar, Jamieson said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
